      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794313005318,
      "created": 1794312973265,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Rate limiter -microservice",
      "fontSize": 145.33333333333357,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Rate limiter -microservice",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "6T_95IevZzXDtsvHi3dHO",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 291.50000000000273,
      "y": 3129.20634920635,
      "width": 800,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0Q",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 429177647,
      "version": 439,
      "versionNonce": 121191233,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794313888600,
      "created": 1794313025219,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- The reverse proxy's purpose is to make\neach requests deterministic, in the sense\nthat we want to send each request to the\nsame Rate limiter -unit every time. This\nshould remove the issue where a requests\nrate limit potentially would scale with the\nrate limiter -unit count, where each request\nis sent to a random unit every time.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- The reverse proxy's purpose is to make each requests deterministic, in the sense that we want to send each request to the same Rate limiter -unit every time. This should remove the issue where a requests rate limit potentially would scale with the rate limiter -unit count, where each request is sent to a random unit every time.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "KVZbHj9Df8XiQAi8rx_Uj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1235.9325396825425,
      "y": 3139.5952380952385,
      "width": 1337.4999999999998,
      "height": 540,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b0R",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 936780207,
      "version": 903,
      "versionNonce": 690995119,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1794314734421,
      "created": 1794313187898,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "- Hash function (something like consistent hashing function I guess:\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consistent_hashing) for sharding, if the load\ngets too large I guess\n- There is apparently also Redis Cluster which handles the hashing and\nrouting, but I'm not sure which way I should lean\n- Any unit might communicate with any shard\n- etcd has the business rules for the Rate limiting -units, each unit\nfetches from there\n    - Probably should have a priority in load: first read etcd, if unavailable \n      read latest from disk, and if those are unavailable have some default  \n      ones in binary (or disk, not sure yet)\n- Algorithm is going to be either token bucket or leaky bucket",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Hash function (something like consistent hashing function I guess: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consistent_hashing) for sharding, if the load gets too large I guess\n- There is apparently also Redis Cluster which handles the hashing and routing, but I'm not sure which way I should lean\n- Any unit might communicate with any shard\n- etcd has the business rules for the Rate limiting -units, each unit fetches from there\n    - Probably should have a priority in load: first read etcd, if unavailable \n      read latest from disk, and if those are unavailable have some default    \n      ones in binary (or disk, not sure yet)\n- Algorithm is going to be either token bucket or leaky bucket",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jLKcjOzn9pfwQLQV_QPJ0",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 233.07539682539937,
      "y": 2881.380952380954,
      "width": 522.5,
      "height": 177.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "#e9ecef",
